# tools/gen/season/reds_ledger_witness.rish -- the reds reach the tree.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/gen/season/reds_ledger_witness.rish
#
# Voice Season v9 - slot 9 - happy_zone_witnesses_first.
#
# Own-reds-immediately has always been law here, and it worked -- reds were named
# the moment they were found. What the law never said is WHERE. A check at v9
# found six reds written into the tree and twenty owned out loud, so fourteen
# lessons were living only in a chat window that closes. work-in-progress/REDS.md
# is the durable home; this witness keeps every row complete and the pin bounded.

say "reds-ledger: Language EN — a red owned out loud is a memory; recorded, a proof."
say "reds-ledger: Style Radiant — three fields per row, no softening."
say "reds-ledger: Lens TAME — the pin's bound is named and checked."

let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/reds_ledger_scan.sh"]
say scan.out
assert scan.out contains "verdict=ok" else "reds-ledger: a row is incomplete or the pin is past bound"
assert scan.ok else "reds-ledger: the verdict reads ok while the status fails — they must agree"

say "GREEN: reds-ledger — every red carries what went wrong, what caught it, what it taught"
